^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
dropped the body
--
N5008 [expr.prim.fold]/1: the assignment operators are fold-operators;
/3: `(e1 op ... op e2)' is a binary fold.  libstdc++ 16's <format>
(format:4210, _S_access) uses `(__u._M_bool = ... = __value)' with at most
one element; the front end reported a parse error there, so every <format>
program failed with GCC 16's headers.  Only the one-element forms are
tested: CBMC's goto conversion cannot take the address of a nested
compound assignment (`(x += a) += b' aborts symex with
"address_arithmetic does not handle side_effect", on bin53 too).  Fails on
bin53 (parse error).  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept the program.
